description:
Found by the Long-life re-triage (epic comment 30). Nothing prunes the archived conversations:
- every fresh restore copies the conversation into tombstones/session_recovery_*.json and into the git directory (harness/watchdog.py fresh_session);
- the chassis writes tombstones/session_<stamp>.json on exit 43;
- an unreadable session becomes corrupt_session_*.json.

They live on the 1 GiB /work tmpfs, which counts against the 3 GB memory limit, and the mirror copies tombstones/ to /telemetry every 5 s. A full /work makes a restore fail with ENOSPC. That exhausts the ladder and forces a reseed, which loses the agent's own tag moves. The git-directory copies also counted against the journal's 256 MiB tar limit.

Addressed on aurora-port by plan 6, Task 5 (bbc4fb7):
- watchdog.prune_archives keeps the newest 20 conversation bodies per directory: tombstones/ within 128 MiB, the git directory within 64 MiB, always including the one just made;
- it runs on every fresh restore (exit 43's included) and once at watchdog start;
- it never touches notes, incarnation messages or the agent's other files;
- the journal's tar excludes the git-directory copies.

This is a named deviation from spec §3 ("watchdog ported as-is"), on John's goal of 2026-10-09; the agent can change the figures. The brief clause awaits John: docs/drafts/WORLD-archives.md.

