Vehicle: #21 (WP08.3 resume) is MERGED. Merge SHA: f44399645fb2633e695a5d758cb5a41f43fb848c (tachyon-beep/space_vehicle main; PR #41; parents 64fc58c and 45f426763280aa1274732fc35f99584b4d7f9ebc). The merge tree is identical to the tested head 45f4267.

Evidence at 45f4267:
- Hosted CI, PR run 38044800034: check 3.12 pass, check 3.13 pass, readiness pass.
- Owner gate, both lanes: 539 passed, 0 skipped; ruff and lint 0; strict 2 (expected).
- Implementer gate: 3× 3.12, 539 each.
- Every commit passes its own suite, except 29becaf (bisect skip, documented in the PR).
- Codex approved round 5 with no P1 or P2. Residuals are #40.

Pin values at the merge SHA:
- tests collected: 539 (README counts 525 test functions);
- `report.refuse(` call sites in tools/check_vehicle.py: 882 (unchanged by #21);
- take the linter changelog row from README at the SHA.
Engine identity changes with every vehicle bump, so adoption is a new world.

For operator docs (from the PR body), exit-3 refusals, each one sentence naming the file:
- both checkpoint generations unusable;
- a record that cannot continue the checkpoint, or a record file that cannot be verified (→ new-world procedure);
- an OSError anywhere on the start path, the configuration's reads included, naming the path and errno;
- a record that cannot be written or cut back after a failed append (the run stops);
- a handle that cannot be closed on the way out, when nothing else failed.

Resume stderr lines:
- "[console] … resumed world … at tick N (checkpoint … at tick M, replayed K, republished R)";
- fall-back to the previous checkpoint;
- root-record rewrite;
- pending.json advisory.

Separate and still open: #39 (the claim race; the fix design is in review, not in this SHA).
